        "article_text_excerpt": "A series of inspections ordered by the government in 2024 revealed serious shortcomings and appalling conditions in Hungarian children’s homes, according to previously concealed inspection reports obtained by Direkt36 through a lawsuit. The reports on the inspections, which were conducted separately in each county, contain several serious findings. They reveal that many children were forced to live in unacceptable conditions—amid mold, in the dark, and surrounded by furniture that posed a risk of injury. In one county, it was revealed that after cases of abuse had come to light, the children were left to cope with their trauma on their own; elsewhere, the investigation highlighted the prevalence of sexual abuse among peers. Perhaps the most shocking case was reported in Bács-Kiskun County. According to the inspection’s findings, children at one of the institutions regularly went hungry because they were not given any food after 6:30 p.m. Because of this, some children were even willing",
